rmediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AKIOKA KOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA YOSHIKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AKIOKA, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, YOSHIKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A rare-earth bond magnet which comprises magnet particles containing a rare earth element and bonded with a binder resin, and contains an antioxidant and a lubricant. The binder resin comprises a high-molecular compound comprising structural units represented by the following formula. (In the formula, X represents a functional group containing nitrogen; Y represents a functional group comprising carbonyl; R represents C6-16 linear or branched alkylene; and Ar represents an aromatic residue.) -X-R-X-Y-Ar-Y-</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un aimant à liaison de terres rares constitué de particules aimantées contenant un élément de terres rares et lié par une résine de liaison et contenant un antioxydant et un lubrifiant. La résine de liaison comprend un composé à masse moléculaire élevé renfermant des unités de construction représentées par la formule suivante, (dans laquelle, X représente un groupe fonctionnel contenant de l'azote; Y un groupe fonctionnel contenant du carbonyle; R C6-16 alkylène linéaire ou ramifié; et Ar un résidu aromatique).-X-R-X-Y-Ar-Y-</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>